    "payload": {
      "arguments": {
        "content": "# Product Comparison Report\n\nSources:\n- Atlas: [source](http://127.0.0.1:54998/atlas) (source_id: `be79021337d344f8ad46de29ea8d12a5`)\n- Birch: [source](http://127.0.0.1:54998/birch) (source_id: `b7dbc38a24cb4110947b573df703a867`)\n- Cedar: [source](http://127.0.0.1:54998/cedar) (source_id: `789dac2dad36459287e90016e46a47b5`)\n\n## Comparison\n\n| Product | Price | Project limit | Retention | Export |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Atlas | 120 USD | 40 projects | 7 days | CSV |\n| Birch | 180 USD | 75 projects | 14 days | JSON |\n| Cedar | 240 USD | 90 projects | 30 days | XML |\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**Best overall value: Atlas.** It has the lowest price and still provides core capabilities, though its project limit and retention are the smallest of the three. Choose **Birch** if you need a better balance between cost and capacity. Choose **Cedar** only if the highest project limit and longest retention are worth the highest price.\n\n## Citations\n\n- Atlas: Price 120 USD; limit 40 projects; retention 7 days; export CSV. [source](http://127.0.0.1:54998/atlas)\n- Birch: Price 180 USD; limit 75 projects; retention 14 days; export JSON. [source](http://127.0.0.1:54998/birch)\n- Cedar: Price 240 USD; limit 90 projects; retention 30 days; export XML. [source](http://127.0.0.1:54998/cedar)\n",
        "media_type": "text/markdown",
